<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Rangiriri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1863">1863</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/invasion-of-the-waikato">Invasion of the Waikato</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Rangiriri was fought on 20–21 November 1863 in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waikato">Waikato</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a>, during the British invasion of the Waikato. General Duncan Cameron's troops attacked a strong Māori defensive line between the Waikato river and a lake and suffered heavy losses in repeated assaults. The next morning the defenders raised a white flag and about 180 were taken prisoner, opening the way to the King movement's centre at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ngaruawahia">Ngāruawāhia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-rangiriri.jpg" alt="Battle of Rangiriri" width="320" height="198" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles Heaphy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_repulse_of_the_royal_navy_storming_party_rangiriri_pa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
